Dear colleagues,

I would like to fit a Dail-Madsen Nmix model using pcountOpen() with year-dependent parameters of recruitment, survival and detection. I feel a bit challenged with how to organize the data with unmarkedFramePCO(). I presume that I have to provide the values of YEAR as an M-by-T matrix of yearlySiteCovs, but then don't I need one version of YEAR for recruitment and survival (with T-1 columns) and another, with T columns, for detection ?

